      "message": "n/a here means that the value of the internal pull resistor is a don\u0027t care because the strong external pull up/pull down resistor means that the gpio level will always read the same regardless of if the internal pull up/down resistor is enabled.\n\nThe last column \u0027bits\u0027 shows what the gpio reads, but I can make that more clear. Bit 1 is what is read when the internal pull resistor is disabled, and bit 0 is what it reads when the internal pull resistor is enabled as shown in the \u0027internal\u0027 column.\n\nI added some additional comments to clarify both points.\n\nI removed the logical column given that it might be confusing and isn\u0027t really referenced in the code below.",
      "parentUuid": "97a04ea7_acb4dace",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 827,
        "startChar": 0,
